---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro'
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro'
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Learn about PrismaLens and our mission to make incident response faster and smarter.">
  <Hero
    title="About PrismaLens"
    subtitle="We're building the future of incident investigation — where AI does the searching and your team does the fixing."
  />
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="space-y-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-foreground">Why We Built This</h2>

      <p>
        At 2:47am on a Tuesday, our payment API started timing out. Revenue dropped
        to zero. The on-call engineer spent 90 minutes jumping between Grafana dashboards,
        grepping logs, and correlating deployment times before finding the cause: a database
        migration that added an unindexed column.
      </p>

      <p>
        That engineer had all the right tools — Prometheus, Grafana, distributed tracing,
        structured logs. The problem wasn't <em>observability</em>. It was
        <span class="text-primary font-semibold">correlation</span>. Connecting the dots
        across systems, timelines, and signal types is cognitive work that takes time and
        drains focus.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong class="text-foreground">PrismaLens automates that correlation.</strong> AI
        agents follow investigation playbooks: query metrics for anomalies, search logs for
        errors, trace requests through services, and build a timeline of what happened. The
        same incident that took 90 minutes manually takes PrismaLens under 2 minutes.
      </p>

      <p>
        We built PrismaLens because we believe incident response should be about
        <em>fixing</em> problems, not <em>finding</em> them. Your observability tools
        already captured the evidence. Let AI do the detective work.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-8">Open Source by Design</h3>

      <p>
        PrismaLens is open source because incident response tools should be transparent.
        You should know exactly how investigations run, what data gets queried, and how
        conclusions are reached. Self-host with Docker Compose and keep full control.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-8">Built for SREs, by SREs</h3>

      <p>
        We're not building another observability platform. You already have Prometheus,
        Grafana, Datadog, New Relic. PrismaLens sits on top, connecting those tools together
        and automating the investigation work that wastes your team's time at 3am.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CTA
    title="Join the community"
    description="PrismaLens is open source. Star us on GitHub, contribute, or just say hello."
    href="https://github.com/prismalens"
    label="View on GitHub"
  />
</BaseLayout>
